{"title":"Distance and displacement: what is the difference","key_idea":"Distance is the full path length travelled; displacement is the straight-line change from start to end point.","method":["Trace the path the object actually takes to find distance.","Measure or draw a straight line from the starting point to the ending point to find displacement.","Remember that distance counts every step; displacement ignores the route."],"worked_example":{"problem":"A child walks 3 metres east, then 2 metres west. What are the distance and displacement?","steps":["Count every step taken: 3 metres plus 2 metres equals 5 metres total distance.","Find where the child ends up compared to the start: started at 0, went to 3, came back to 1, so displacement is 1 metre east."],"answer":"Distance = 5 metres; displacement = 1 metre east."},"key_terms":[{"term":"distance","meaning":"the total length of the path actually travelled"},{"term":"displacement","meaning":"the shortest straight-line distance and direction from start to finish"},{"term":"direction","meaning":"the line or way something moves, like north, south, east or west"}],"common_mistakes":["Thinking distance and displacement are always the same number.","Forgetting to include direction when stating displacement.","Counting only the final position instead of the full path for distance."],"remember":"Distance is how far you go; displacement is how far you end up from where you started.","quick_check":[{"q":"A ball rolls 6 metres north then 1 metre south. What is the distance?","a":"7 metres."},{"q":"A ball rolls 6 metres north then 1 metre south. What is the displacement?","a":"5 metres north."}],"tell_your_child":"Imagine you walk to the store and back home — the distance is the full walk there and back, but your displacement is zero because you ended up where you started. Distance is about the journey; displacement is about where you really ended up.","picture":{"concept_key":"c5-physics-distance-displacement","scene_prompt":"A child standing at a starting point, walking along a wavy path to a destination, with a straight arrow showing the direct line back."}}
